WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.280
Hi, I'm Hap.

2
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.600
Today we're opening the browser console,

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.480
and reading the error that turns up when a
page asks for a file and doesn't get one.

4
00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:18.742
Here's a page you've just opened
by double-clicking the file.

5
00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:21.062
The heading is there and
the styling is there,

6
00:00:21.062 --> 00:00:24.342
so the HTML parsed and the CSS applied.

7
00:00:24.422 --> 00:00:26.502
But it still says loading the notes,

8
00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:30.827
and it's going to say that forever
because the file it needs never arrived.

9
00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:34.187
When errors like this occur,
they are written to the console.

10
00:00:34.427 --> 00:00:37.307
To see the console, you
have to open DevTools.

11
00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:41.627
One way to do that is to right-click
anywhere on the page and choose Inspect.

12
00:00:43.362 --> 00:00:48.242
What opens is the Chrome DevTools'
Elements panel that shows the HTML.

13
00:00:48.402 --> 00:00:50.562
Across the top you'll
see the tabs of other

14
00:00:50.562 --> 00:00:53.522
panels and to see the errors,
click on the Console tab.

15
00:00:55.076 --> 00:00:59.396
The console is where the browser
writes messages while the page runs.

16
00:00:59.636 --> 00:01:02.996
It writes them as they happen
rather than keeping a record,

17
00:01:03.076 --> 00:01:06.916
so anything that went wrong before
you opened it may already be gone.

18
00:01:07.156 --> 00:01:08.676
So always reload the page.

19
00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:12.247
So here's what it wrote.

20
00:01:12.247 --> 00:01:15.847
Red means the browser tried
to do something and couldn't.

21
00:01:16.087 --> 00:01:18.807
Read the first red line
rather than the last one,

22
00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:23.767
because the ones underneath are
usually the same problem arriving
again with a different name.

23
00:01:24.368 --> 00:01:28.528
This one says it failed to fetch, and
then it names the file it wanted.

24
00:01:30.487 --> 00:01:33.767
That failure is why sites
need to run a server.

25
00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:37.607
Fetching is one part of a
page asking for another file,

26
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:41.287
and that request needs something
on the other end to answer it.

27
00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.487
Open the file straight off your
disk and there's no server,

28
00:01:44.722 --> 00:01:49.762
so the request fails and the piece
that depended on it never fills in.

29
00:01:50.082 --> 00:01:53.202
The server is the thing on
the other end that answers,

30
00:01:53.362 --> 00:01:55.362
which is why you run one while you work.

31
00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:56.770
That's it.

32
00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.770
Leave DevTools open while you work, and
you'll see errors when they happen.
